# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable via `graphify update .`)
/graphify-out

# .cargo/config.toml is committed: it carries the `cargo xtask` alias the CI
# jobs depend on (SL-0.WS.01). User-level overrides live in CARGO_HOME, not here.


# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Python / misc tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Corpus PDFs — fetched via `xtask corpus fetch`, never committed (SL-0.CORP.01)
/corpus/pdfs/

tmp_*

# cargo-fuzz output (SL-0.SEC.02)
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/coverage/
/fuzz/artifacts/

# pnpm / node (SL-0.WS.10)
node_modules/
dist/
target-agent/
/target-ci
# Lazy fallback-font payloads (SL-3.FONT.12): the 10 non-built-in Liberation
# faces, brotli-compressed. Regenerable byte-for-byte from the committed
# sources in assets/fonts/ by cargo xtask fallback-assets, and ~0.7 MB of
# binaries in git buys nothing the manifest does not already pin. Same rule the
# CJK payload follows: the manifest is committed, the chunks are built.
assets/payload/fallback/*.ttf.br

# Local agent scratch (build logs, probes, patches). Never committed.
.kilo/

# The web app's generated deployment root (SL-4.WEB.02). The COMMITTED parts of
# `apps/web/host/public/` are the hand-written shell — index.html, _headers,
# assets/boot.js, assets/style.css — plus whatever `tools/place-sw.mjs` emits
# (sw.js and the modules it imports). What `tools/place-assets.mjs` emits is
# build output copied out of other packages' dist/ and the cargo target dir:
#
#   assets/ui/**, assets/ui-kit/**  the viewer, copied from apps/ui/dist and
#                                   packages/ui-kit/dist by an import walk
#   wasm/selis_pdf_wasm.wasm        the engine, copied from the cargo target dir
#   app-manifest.json               the list of what was copied
#
# None of it is authored here, and committing it would put a 2.8 MB binary and
# 35 copied modules in the tree that a reviewer cannot meaningfully read and
# that silently goes stale against its source. The extension already follows
# this rule (SL-0.LEGAL.04): artefacts are built and manifested, not committed.
apps/web/host/public/assets/ui/
apps/web/host/public/assets/ui-kit/
apps/web/host/public/wasm/
apps/web/host/public/app-manifest.json
